<title>USA: Diametrics sees narrower 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>Diametrics sees narrower 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diametrics Medical Inc chief executive David Giddings said Wednesday he expects the company will lose less than the $22 million projected by Wall Street analysts for 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;We'll come in, I believe, more favorable than that,&quot; he said in an interview at a Dain Bosworth conference here.</p>
<p>Dain Bosworth had projected a 1996 loss for Diametrics of $22.4 million, compared to a loss of $23 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Giddings said this year's loss would be smaller due to cost reductions made by the company.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
